[profiles.guide]
notes = '''Hold {select} and {start} together to pause the gyro while you reposition the controller. Tilting the controller moves the pointer, as a fine pointer next to the right stick {rs}.
The game has no controller support, so this plays it with the mouse and keys, one scheme for every stage and editor. The right stick {rs} moves the pointer and the left stick {ls} swims, walks or flies (W A S D). {rt} or {south} clicks: move there, eat, attack, socialize, pick a part; {lt} right-clicks, and in the editors holding it and moving the pointer turns the creature.
{east} jumps (Space). Hold {north} (the middle button) and move the pointer to turn the camera; {up} and {down} zoom. Hold {rb} and point the right stick {rs} for the 1 to 0 keys: abilities in the creature and tribal stages, tools in space.
In the editors {left} undoes and {right} redoes, {west} {color:red}deletes{/color} the part in hand. {start} is the menu and backs out. Naming a creature or a planet: {guide} + {west} opens the on-screen keyboard.
Spore can't remap its keys, and these are its remembered defaults, not checked on an install: Space for jump, the middle button for the camera and Delete in the editors most of all.'''

